# Lists

Use a list to break text into short pieces that are quick to scan. Use a real list, not bullet characters typed into a paragraph. Screen readers announce a real list and how many items it has.

How to word a list, with a lead-in line and the right punctuation, is on [Text formatting](../content/formatting-content/text-formatting.html#lists).

## Bulleted lists

Use a bulleted list when the order of the items does not matter. In a Markdown card, start each item with a hyphen.

```yaml
type: markdown
content: |
  Before you go away, check that:

  - the back door is locked
  - the heating is set to frost protection
  - the porch light is on its timer
```

## Numbered lists

Use a numbered list for steps that people must follow in order.

```yaml
type: markdown
content: |
  To reset the hall motion sensor:

  1. Take out the battery.
  2. Hold the button for 5 seconds.
  3. Put the battery back in.
```

## Long list items

Set list items in body text, the same size as paragraphs. Let a long item wrap onto the next line. Do not cut it off, and do not make the text smaller to fit.

If most items run over 2 lines, the list is hard to scan. Shorten the items, or split the list under 2 headings.
